course: dictionary
lesson: 327
title: One word, three meanings: Angus
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and you can tell which one a writer means by reading the clues around it. The word angus is a good example. It can be a name, a place, or a kind of cattle.
explain: «In Hull, Angus's dad stays in bed for days with the curtains shut.» Here Angus has an apostrophe and 's', so it is a person's name. Angus is a Scottish boy's name, and the sentence is about a family, so the name fits.
explain: Now think about a farm or a butcher's shop. If someone talks about Angus beef, the clue is beef, so Angus means a breed of black or red cattle with no horns. Always ask yourself: which meaning makes sense in this sentence?
fact: Angus is a proper noun, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Angus cattle are black or red, have no horns, and come from Scotland.
fact: Angus beef is famous and is often used in burgers.
fact: Angus is also an area in eastern Scotland, called a council area.
fact: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if the sentence still makes sense, you have chosen well.
exercise: «In Hull, Angus's dad stays in bed for days.» In this sentence, what is Angus? | A kind of beef burger | A breed of cattle | *A boy's name | A council area in Scotland
exercise: A farmer says, «We sell Angus beef at the market.» What does Angus mean here? | A council area in eastern Scotland | A type of toast | *A breed of black or red cattle with no horns | A boy's name
exercise: Ella reads, «Angus is a council area in eastern Scotland.» Which clue tells you Angus is a place? | The word is short | Angus is capitalised | *Council area in eastern Scotland | Angus is a name
test: Which country does Angus cattle come from? | Wales | Ireland | *Scotland | England
test: «Rafferty's mum stays in her room, so every arvo (afternoon) he makes toast.» What does arvo mean? | *Afternoon | Morning | Bedtime | Lunch
exam: Which meaning of Angus fits best in «Angus is famous for black cattle with no horns»? | A council area | A kind of toast | *A breed of cattle | A boy's name
